  "articleBody": "Cabinet replacement is a major investment, and understanding the main cost drivers helps you build a realistic budget before demo starts.\n\nKey Decision Factors:\n- Cabinet Construction: Stock, semi-custom, or custom cabinets vary widely in price. Solid wood face frames, plywood boxes, and soft-close hardware cost more than basic laminate or particleboard, but they provide greater durability over time.\n- Layout Changes: Keeping your existing footprint minimizes costs. Shifting your sink, range, or refrigerator requires rough plumbing and electrical alterations, which adds labor and may trigger local permit and inspection requirements.\n- Countertop Coordination: Replacing base cabinets almost always requires new countertops. Factoring in stone fabrication, templating, and plumbing reconnection ensures there are no surprises in your bottom line.\n- Wall and Subfloor Repairs: Removing old cabinets sometimes uncovers hidden water damage, mold, or out-of-plumb walls that need carpentry and drywall repair before new boxes can be installed safely.\n\nWhat to Do Next:\nAsk your contractor for a comprehensive estimate that accounts for demolition, disposal, cabinet installation, trim carpentry, and utility coordination. Abraham Becerra and HH Remodeling LLC deliver transparent estimates and hands-on craftsmanship for homeowners throughout Denver, Aurora, and surrounding communities. Call 303-505-0866 to discuss your kitchen replacement project.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
